  "question": {
    "text": "According to Bohr's model, the minimum energy (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>eV</mi></math>)&nbsp;required to remove an electron from the ground state of a doubly ionized&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Li</mi></math> atom <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is",
